The 9110 uses a completely different operating system, and probably
doesn't have the resources anyway. One interesting experiment could be
to try an MS-DOS Nethack or some of the various other DOS roguelikes
under DOS:
        http://dchapman.com/freeware/dos9k/index.html

The 9110 is very much an embedded PC and a mobile phone in a single
package, you can even boot it to some embedded DOS. It isn't really
hardware compatible though, but applications that stick to BIOS calls
might work.


